// [category, title, takeaway, deeper explanation, reflection, source key, location]
const rows=[
['Psychology','Why a tiny reward changes what you do next','A consequence can shape whether a behavior happens again.','Reinforcement is defined by its effect on future behavior, not by whether someone intended it as a reward. If opening a book regularly leads to an enjoyable experience, that pattern may become easier to repeat.','What pleasant experience could follow two pages of reading?','learning','Reinforcement'],
['Philosophy','What is actually yours to control?','Epictetus separates our choices from outcomes we cannot command.','Stoic practice begins by distinguishing judgments and intentions from external events. This does not require indifference to other people; it asks us to act responsibly without pretending that every result is ours to decide.','Which part of your current difficulty is within your influence?','stoic','Section 1'],
['Faith','The strength nobody can see','Proverbs places self-control above the conquest of a city.','The image reverses ordinary ideas about power. The ability to restrain anger and govern one’s response is presented as a greater achievement than outward victory. This is a wisdom teaching, not a promise that restraint guarantees success.','Where would restraint be stronger than retaliation?','bible','Proverbs 16:32'],
['Science','The Moon is not changing shape','Lunar phases are changes in the illuminated portion we see from Earth.','The Sun lights roughly half the Moon. As the Moon moves around Earth, our viewing angle changes. A crescent is not normally caused by Earth’s shadow; that is involved in a lunar eclipse.','Look at the Moon tonight and estimate where the Sun is.','moon','Moon phases'],
['Learning','Your memory needs a workout, not a replay','Trying to recall an idea can reveal whether you really know it.','After reading, close the page and reconstruct the main argument. Compare your answer with the original. The effort exposes gaps that familiar-looking sentences may conceal.','Explain the last thing you read without looking at it.','memory','Retrieval and rehearsal'],
['Family','A small conversation is a big investment','Responsive exchanges help support a young child’s development.','A child points, makes a sound or looks at something. An attentive adult responds, allowing a back-and-forth exchange. These ordinary interactions offer practice in communication and relationships. They do not need to be elaborate lessons.','Follow a child’s interest for a few minutes without your phone.','family','Serve and return'],
['Finance','The price is not the whole cost','Even a small purchase uses resources and attention.','A spending record reveals patterns that memory can miss. A bargain may be worthwhile, but its value depends on use, available money and alternatives. A budget is a way of assigning limited resources deliberately.','What purchase would you still choose without a discount?','finance','Spending assessment'],
['Character','Practice the person you intend to become','Actions are a more concrete training ground than aspirations.','Marcus Aurelius repeatedly turns attention toward conduct in the present. His notebooks are exercises in remembering principles when daily life makes them difficult to follow. The point is not to appear philosophical but to act accordingly.','Name one action that would express your values today.','marcus','Books II and V'],
['Health','Movement pays dividends beyond appearance','Physical activity benefits more than muscles and body weight.','Regular activity supports health, and even a single session can produce some benefits. The CDC identifies improvements in areas such as sleep and anxiety. A manageable routine is a practical starting point rather than an all-or-nothing test.','Choose a short walk you can realistically take today.','health','Immediate and long-term benefits'],
['Psychology','Why clever people can defend poor decisions','Reasoning can be used to justify a choice already made.','Cognitive dissonance describes the discomfort that can follow inconsistency between attitudes and behavior. People may change their conduct, revise beliefs or justify what happened. Being able to give a reason is not proof that the reason is sound.','Which belief would you be willing to revise if evidence changed?','persuasion','Cognitive dissonance'],
['Learning','Connect new ideas to old ones','Meaningful associations can help make information memorable.','Instead of memorizing a definition alone, connect it to an experience or concept you already understand. This makes several possible routes back to the idea. A good analogy can help, but it should not hide important differences.','Make an analogy for one unfamiliar idea.','memory','Elaborative rehearsal'],
['Science','A day on Venus is surprisingly long','Venus rotates exceptionally slowly compared with Earth.','Its spin is retrograde relative to most planets, and one rotation relative to distant stars takes longer than one orbit around the Sun. A solar day is a different measurement because it also depends on orbital motion.','Why are a rotation and a sunrise-to-sunrise day different?','planets','Venus'],
['Faith','Listening before answering','James associates mature conduct with listening and restraint.','James 1:19–20 links readiness to hear with caution in speaking and anger. The passage sits in a letter concerned with lived faith. It invites reflection on how reactions affect relationships.','In your next disagreement, listen fully before replying.','bible','James 1:19–20'],
['Philosophy','Do not confuse reputation with character','Being thought admirable and acting admirably are different goals.','Epictetus treats reputation as something partly outside our control. A person can choose honesty and care, but cannot guarantee how those choices will be interpreted. The distinction can help clarify decisions made under social pressure.','Would you do the right thing if nobody noticed?','stoic','Sections 1 and 13'],
['Family','Notice what the child notices','Attention can be shared rather than commanded.','When an adult follows a child’s focus, the child has a meaningful reason to communicate. Naming an object or responding to a gesture can turn an ordinary moment into an exchange. This is not a requirement to entertain children continuously.','Describe something your child is already looking at.','family','Responsive interaction'],
['Finance','A budget is a decision made in advance','Planning makes tradeoffs visible before money disappears.','Record income and actual expenses, then include irregular costs and savings goals. A realistic plan should reflect how life actually works, not merely how one wishes to spend. Adjust when circumstances change.','Which recurring cost surprised you recently?','finance','Budgeting'],
['Health','A little movement still counts','Healthful activity need not begin with a perfect training program.','Moving more and sitting less can be useful even when a person cannot immediately achieve formal activity targets. Progress can be gradual. The appropriate activity depends on physical ability and medical circumstances.','What is the easiest safe way to move more today?','health','Activity benefits'],
['Psychology','Not every convincing message contains a good argument','Persuasion can work through cues unrelated to evidence.','A message may persuade through careful consideration of its claims or through impressions such as attractiveness, credibility cues and presentation. These are not identical processes. A polished presentation should prompt evaluation rather than automatic agreement.','What evidence supports the next persuasive post you encounter?','persuasion','Routes to persuasion'],
['Literature','A Roman emperor’s private notebook','Meditations is less a manifesto than a repeated exercise in reflection.','The work is associated with Marcus Aurelius in the second century CE. Its recurring themes suggest a person returning to principles rather than someone who mastered them once and never struggled again.','What principle would you write down to remember tomorrow?','marcus','Read the original work'],
['Science','Why Pluto changed categories','Pluto did not physically change when its planetary classification changed.','Scientific classifications are conventions designed to organize evidence. The discovery of additional bodies in the outer solar system helped motivate a clearer definition of planet. Pluto remains an important world to study.','Can a definition change without the object itself changing?','planets','Planet classification'],
['Learning','Read with a question in mind','A purpose can turn passive reading into active interpretation.','Before starting a chapter, formulate a question. While reading, connect the answer to what you already know. Afterward, explain it in your own words. This is an application of elaborative learning rather than a guarantee of perfect recall.','Write one question before your next reading session.','memory','Elaborative rehearsal'],
['Faith','What does wisdom look like in action?','James challenges readers to demonstrate faith in conduct.','James 1:22–25 contrasts hearing with doing. The mirror illustration presents self-awareness without action as incomplete. This is a theological exhortation, not a scientific theory of habit formation.','What teaching do you already know but need to practice?','bible','James 1:22–25'],
['Character','Anger is not your only possible response','A pause creates room to choose how to act.','In Stoic ethics, an initial impression is not identical to an endorsed judgment. Epictetus encourages examining the impression rather than immediately accepting it. Modern readers can use this as a reflection exercise, not as a claim that emotions are voluntary.','What interpretation could you check before responding?','stoic','Section 5'],
['Science','A solar system is more than planets','Our neighborhood also contains moons, asteroids and comets.','Small bodies preserve clues about the early solar system. Some never became part of planets. The diversity of objects reminds us that the familiar eight-planet diagram is only a simplified view.','Which kind of small solar-system body interests you?','space','Small bodies'],
['Psychology','Removing discomfort can reinforce an action','Relief can help explain repeated avoidance.','Negative reinforcement means that a behavior becomes more likely because something unpleasant is removed. It is not the same as punishment. If checking a phone relieves boredom, that relief may help maintain the checking habit.','What feeling usually comes just before you reach for your phone?','learning','Negative reinforcement'],
['Family','A response does not need to be perfect','Ordinary attentive exchanges matter more than elaborate activities.','Caregivers can support communication through eye contact, gestures, words and attention. Real households have interruptions and competing demands. The practical aim is repeated responsiveness rather than continuous performance.','Find one small moment for undistracted attention.','family','Responsive relationships'],
['Finance','Track the purchases that disappear into the background','Small and infrequent expenses are easy to overlook.','Review recent transactions rather than relying on impressions. Group purchases by purpose, and include nonmonthly costs. This gives a more useful baseline for choosing spending priorities.','Review the last five discretionary transactions.','finance','Reviewing spending'],
['Health','Exercise and sleep are connected','Movement can be one contributor to better sleep.','Physical activity has evidence-based benefits for sleep quality. It is not a guaranteed cure for insomnia or a reason to cut sleep short. Rest, timing and medical factors also matter.','What routine could support both activity and rest?','health','Sleep benefits'],
['Learning','Recognition is not the same as recall','A sentence looking familiar does not mean you can explain it.','Recognition provides cues that free recall does not. To assess understanding, try answering a question without the source, then check what was missing. Familiarity is useful but insufficient by itself.','Summarize this post from memory in one sentence.','memory','Memory strategies'],
['Philosophy','A useful distinction when plans fail','Your chosen response is different from the event that interrupts your plans.','Stoicism does not ask us to stop planning. It asks us to recognize that events can depart from plans and to focus on acting well under the conditions actually present. This is a philosophical position, not a clinical prescription.','How could you respond constructively to a disrupted plan?','stoic','Sections 1 and 8'],
['Faith','The hidden architecture of a life','Jesus compares hearing and acting on his teaching to building on rock.','Matthew ends the Sermon on the Mount with two builders. The contrast is not between hearing and ignorance but between acting and failing to act. The passage is a theological image about discipleship.','What would building on this teaching mean in practice?','bible','Matthew 7:24–27'],
['Science','The solar system has worlds with many moons','A planet can have a whole system of smaller orbiting bodies.','Moons differ widely in size and composition. Some are scientifically compelling in their own right, including worlds studied for possible subsurface oceans. A planet is often a starting point for exploration rather than the entire story.','Choose a moon you would like to learn about.','space','Moons'],
['History','Why an emperor wrote about everyday conduct','A powerful political office did not eliminate the need for self-reflection.','Marcus Aurelius ruled the Roman Empire in the second century CE. Reading his notes alongside that historical setting helps separate his actual writings from modern slogans attributed to him. His philosophy is one perspective, not a complete account of Roman society.','What changes when you read an author in historical context?','history','Author and historical context'],
['Psychology','Can a habit survive unreliable rewards?','Different reinforcement patterns can produce different patterns of responding.','Operant conditioning research examines schedules in which consequences occur after varying numbers of responses or periods of time. These models can help frame questions about digital habits, but they do not establish that every social media user is addicted.','Which app rewards your checking inconsistently?','learning','Reinforcement schedules'],
['Family','Words attach meaning to shared experience','Naming what a child notices can support communication.','A caregiver can describe a passing vehicle, an animal or a feeling when the child shows interest. The exchange makes words relevant to an experience already attracting attention. Follow the child’s cues instead of demanding a lesson.','Name and describe something during a shared activity.','family','Serve and return'],
['Finance','Savings deserve their own line','A savings goal is easier to evaluate when it appears explicitly in a plan.','A budget can include planned saving alongside bills and regular costs. This makes the tradeoff between current spending and future priorities visible. The appropriate amount depends on income, obligations and circumstances.','Which future expense should you plan for now?','finance','Savings in a budget'],
['Learning','Explain it to an imaginary beginner','A simple explanation tests the structure of your understanding.','Connecting an idea to familiar examples is a form of elaboration. If you cannot explain how the parts relate, you may have memorized terms without understanding the concept. Return to the source to resolve the gap.','Explain a concept you learned today to a beginner.','memory','Elaboration'],
['Faith','Ambition and service are not identical','Paul urges believers to consider the interests of others.','Philippians 2:3–4 addresses communal life and humility. It challenges self-centered motivation rather than providing a universal career rule. Read the following verses to understand the theological example used in the letter.','How might an ambition serve someone besides yourself?','bible','Philippians 2:3–11'],
['Science','Earth is a rocky planet, not a miniature Jupiter','The planets are not all built from the same materials.','The inner planets are terrestrial worlds with rocky compositions. Jupiter and Saturn are gas giants, while Uranus and Neptune are ice giants. These categories describe broad physical differences, not perfectly uniform worlds.','Compare Earth and Jupiter using the NASA planet guide.','planets','Planet types'],
['Character','The next useful action','A large ideal can be approached through one concrete choice.','In Meditations, attention frequently returns to the duties of the present. A modern application is to identify the next worthwhile action instead of dwelling exclusively on an imagined future identity. This is a reflective interpretation.','What is the next useful thing you can do?','marcus','Books V and VI'],
['Psychology','Mental categories are useful, but imperfect','Concepts help organize experience and reduce complexity.','We use categories to recognize patterns and reason about unfamiliar objects. But real examples do not always fit neatly into a single category. Treat categories as useful tools, not substitutes for examining a particular case.','When has a label hidden an important difference?','cognition','Concepts and prototypes'],
['Health','Think in years, not just workouts','Regular movement supports multiple dimensions of long-term health.','Physical activity is associated with benefits across cardiovascular, metabolic and functional health. It is useful to think beyond short-term changes in appearance. Choose sustainable activities appropriate to your circumstances.','Which activity could you realistically continue for years?','health','Long-term benefits'],
['Literature','Read the source before the quotation card','Context can change the meaning of a memorable sentence.','An isolated line from an ancient philosophical text can obscure its argument. Reading the preceding and following sections helps reveal the assumptions and purpose of the passage. Different translations can also use different words.','Read one complete section of Epictetus instead of a quote.','stoic','Read the original work'],
['History','Psychology did not begin with one school','The field developed through competing ways of studying mind and behavior.','The history of psychology includes approaches that emphasized conscious experience, observable behavior and other questions. Modern psychology is not reducible to any single early school. Understanding the history helps interpret claims about human nature.','Which question is better answered by observation than introspection?','psychology','History of psychology'],
['Faith','Words can build or damage relationships','Proverbs repeatedly treats speech as morally consequential.','Proverbs 15:1 contrasts a gentle response with harsh speech. It is wisdom literature: a general insight about conduct, not a guarantee that every conflict can be resolved by gentleness.','Where could a calmer answer improve a conversation?','bible','Proverbs 15:1'],
['Science','A comet is a visitor with a changing appearance','Comets become more conspicuous when solar heating releases material.','Comets contain volatile material and dust. As they approach the Sun, released gas and dust can form a coma and tails. Their appearance changes as the conditions around them change.','What makes a comet different from an asteroid?','space','Comets'],
['Finance','Separate needs from priorities','A useful budget reflects deliberate choices rather than moral labels.','Start from actual obligations and spending. Some discretionary expenses may support genuine priorities, while others may be easy to reduce. The goal is to direct resources where they matter most, not to eliminate all enjoyment.','Which expense brings lasting value to you?','finance','Assessing spending'],
['Psychology','Praise is not always reinforcement','The result of a consequence matters more than its label.','If praise increases a behavior, it functions as reinforcement in that situation. If it does not, it may not have that function. The same consequence can affect different people differently.','What actually makes your reading behavior more likely?','learning','Positive reinforcement'],
['Philosophy','A disagreement is an opportunity to examine a judgment','Stoic reflection begins with questioning how we interpret events.','Epictetus distinguishes events from the judgments people form about them. This does not make harms unreal or remove responsibility. It invites examination of the mental steps between encountering an event and deciding how to respond.','What assumption are you making about another person’s motives?','stoic','Section 5'],
['Learning','Build a knowledge network, not a pile of facts','A concept becomes more useful when connected to other ideas.','Elaborative rehearsal makes relationships between new and existing knowledge explicit. After learning about reinforcement, for example, compare it with persuasion and ask where the concepts overlap and differ. Connections should clarify rather than erase distinctions.','Link two discoveries from this feed.','memory','Elaborative rehearsal']
];
